  "narrative": "I assessed all newly delivered discovery evidence against the prespecified clinical-support rule: because the dependency-score means are negative, the 10% benchmark was set at 10% of the absolute outcome mean, and an accept required the signed 95% interval lower bound to reach that benchmark. No new result satisfies this rule. Feature_032 coherence is mixed and not clinically interval-supported. H157 (outcome_006) is opposite the claimed direction, but its upper bound exceeds the 0.0176 benchmark, so I mark it unresolved closed rather than reject. H242 (outcome_011) has a point estimate above the 0.0301 benchmark, but the lower bound is far below it. H243 (outcome_001) is also opposite the claimed direction, with an upper bound still above the 0.0415 benchmark, so it remains unresolved closed. These coherence tests do not establish a coherent feature_032 pattern, but they also do not eliminate the direct outcome_014 candidate H144. H144 remains the only main-effect candidate near clinical support: signed estimate about 0.0685 with lower bound about -0.0012. Because prior validation of a related feature_032 subgroup was null and coherence is inconsistent, validation of the main H144 contrast is the most informative next step before either acceptance or closure. I request validation of H144. Feature_045 reversal coherence fails or is nonclinical. H239 and H240 are below their outcome-specific benchmarks with negative lower bounds; H244 is extremely imprecise. H245 rejects a clinically meaningful positive reversal on outcome_001 because its upper bound is below the benchmark; H246 and H247 reject on outcome_012 and outcome_015 because their signed estimates are opposite and upper bounds are below benchmark. I therefore close the feature_045 reversal line, leaving H104 unresolved but closed because the direct outcome_014 interval still includes clinically meaningful values; it is not supportable as a discovery-level association. H131 (feature_050 on outcome_014) is not supported and is closed after considering its near-boundary outcome_015 and subgroup evidence. The feature_055 line produced one zero-excluding positive result: H248 on outcome_008 has signed estimate 0.0315, above the 0.0282 benchmark, but its lower bound 0.0018 is well below benchmark, so it is unresolved active rather than acceptable. H249 on outcome_011 is essentially null, although its upper bound just reaches the 0.0301 benchmark, so it is unresolved closed. Because H144 is the central pre-identified candidate and only one voluntary validation is allowed now, I did not validate H248 yet; it remains active as a possible next validation if H144 fails. Overall, there are no newly accepted associations, and all conclusions remain dataset-specific associations rather than causal or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 15 appraise state. Supported set remains empty. Validation requested: H144 only. Critical rule: accept only if signed discovery lower bound reaches outcome benchmark: outcome_014 ~0.0093, outcome_013 ~0.0269, outcome_011 ~0.0301, outcome_008 ~0.0282, outcome_001 ~0.0415, outcome_012 ~0.0248, outcome_015 ~0.0250, outcome_006 ~0.0176. No new result meets accept rule. H144 feature_032/outcome_014 remains active central candidate: direct lower -0.0012, point 0.0685, but prior subgroup validation null and coherence mixed (H157 opposite, H242 imprecise positive, H243 opposite). Validation H144 next. If validation lower bound reaches benchmark, accept H144; if null/nonclinical, reject/close feature_032 main line. Feature_045 line closed: H104 direct not clinical; coherence failures H245/246/247 reject positive reversal on outcome_001/012/015, H239/240 below benchmark, H244 imprecise. H104 left unresolved closed because direct interval includes clinical values but line unsupported. Feature_050 line closed: H131 nonclinical and inconsistent with prior near-boundary/subgroup evidence. Feature_055 line active: H248 outcome_008 level_001 vs level_003 is zero-excluding and clinically by point estimate, lower bound 0.0018 below benchmark; H249 outcome_011 near null. Keep H248 active as possible next validation if H144 fails. Avoid accepting or over-interpreting post-selection zero-exclusion results without coherence or validation.",
